{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Fast sparse regression for high-dimensional data",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A. Student",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Department of Computer Science, University of Somewhere",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Affiliation"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sparse linear models are a workhorse of data analysis, but fitting them on datasets with millions of features remains slow. This thesis presents a proximal gradient algorithm whose cost per iteration is linear in the size of the data and which converges at the optimal rate for first-order methods. On four benchmark datasets it improves accuracy by 4 to 7 percentage points over three baselines at equal running time. We also give a convergence proof and a study of its limitations.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Acknowledgements",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": false,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "I thank my supervisor, Prof. J. Supervisor, for her guidance throughout this work, the members of the optimisation group for many fruitful discussions, and the Somewhere Research Council for funding under grant SRC-2022-114. Above all I thank my family.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\tableofcontents",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "ch:intro",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Background and motivation",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Regularised regression is among the most widely used statistical tools. When the number of features ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "d",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is large, the lasso ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "tibs1996"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " selects a small subset of them by penalising the ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\ell_1",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " norm of the coefficients. Genomics, text classification and online advertising routinely produce problems with ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "d > 10^6",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", where even one pass over the data is expensive.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Research questions",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This thesis addresses three questions:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Can the lasso be fitted with a cost per iteration linear in the number of non-zero entries of the data?",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Does the resulting algorithm retain the optimal convergence rate of first-order methods?",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "How does it compare in accuracy with established solvers on standard benchmarks?",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Thesis outline",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Chapter 2 reviews the literature and Chapter 3 presents the algorithm and its analysis. Chapter 4 reports experiments (see Table ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "tab:results",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " and Figure ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "fig:conv",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": "), Chapter 5 discusses them, and Chapter 6 concludes.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Literature review",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sparse regression",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Given a design matrix ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "X \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n\\times d}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and a response ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "y \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the lasso solves",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\beta^{*} = \\arg\\min_{\\beta}\\ \\tfrac{1}{2}\\|X\\beta - y\\|_2^2 + \\lambda\\|\\beta\\|_1 ,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:lasso",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "with ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda > 0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " controlling sparsity. Least-angle regression ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "efron2004"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " traces the whole solution path but needs cubic time in the number of active features.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "First-order methods",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Coordinate descent ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "friedman2010"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " and proximal gradient methods ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "beck2009"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " avoid matrix factorisations. Accelerated proximal gradient attains the optimal ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "O(1/t^2)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " rate, but each iteration touches the full matrix.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Identified gap",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "No published solver combines a per-iteration cost proportional to the data sparsity with the accelerated rate and a guarantee on the selected support. Closing this gap is the aim of the thesis.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Methodology",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Problem formulation",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We study Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:lasso",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " under the assumption that ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "X",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " has ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "m",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " non-zero entries, so one multiplication by ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "X",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " costs ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "O(m)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Let ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "L",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " be the largest eigenvalue of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "X^\\top X",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The algorithm",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Algorithm ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "alg:pgd",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " applies soft-thresholding after each gradient step of size ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "1/L",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\begin{algorithm}[H]\n\\SetAlgoLined\n\\KwIn{$X$, $y$, $\\lambda$, step size $\\eta = 1/L$, iterations $T$}\n\\KwOut{Coefficients $\\beta_T$}\n$\\beta_0 \\leftarrow 0$\\;\n\\For{$t = 1$ \\KwTo $T$}{\n  $g_t \\leftarrow X^\\top (X\\beta_{t-1} - y)$\\;\n  $\\beta_t \\leftarrow \\mathrm{soft}(\\beta_{t-1} - \\eta g_t,\\ \\eta\\lambda)$\\;\n}\n\\caption{Proximal gradient for the lasso}\n\\label{alg:pgd}\n\\end{algorithm}",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Convergence",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "kind": "proposition",
      "title": "Convergence rate",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Let ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "F(\\beta)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " be the objective of Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:lasso",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Then Algorithm 1 satisfies ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "F(\\beta_t)-F(\\beta^*) \\le \\dfrac{L\\|\\beta^*\\|_2^2}{2t}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "start": true,
      "type": "Theorem"
    },
    {
      "kind": "proof",
      "title": "",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The bound follows from the standard descent lemma for the smooth part and the non-expansiveness of the proximal map; see Appendix ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "app:proof",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "start": true,
      "type": "Theorem"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Adding momentum improves the rate to ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "O(1/t^2)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", at the price of one extra vector.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Implementation",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The algorithm was implemented in Python 3.12 with NumPy and SciPy sparse matrices. Experiments ran on a workstation with 64 GB of memory. The stopping tolerance was ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\epsilon = 10^{-6}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and the iteration limit ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "T = 10{,}000",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Results",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
