          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A. Author",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radioactive decay",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "ch:decay",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "An unstable nucleus transforms into another one at a moment that nothing in its past predicts. Yet a large sample of identical nuclei decays with perfect regularity. This chapter derives that regularity, defines the quantities used to measure it, and applies them to a medical radioisotope generator. The treatment follows the standard approach of introductory nuclear physics texts ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "example2019",
            "sample2021"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The decay law",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Suppose a sample contains ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N(t)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " nuclei at time ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "t",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Each nucleus has the same probability per unit time ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " of decaying, independent of its age and of its surroundings. In a short interval ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\mathrm{d}t",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " the number of decays is therefore proportional to the number of nuclei present,",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\frac{\\mathrm{d}N}{\\mathrm{d}t} = -\\lambda N,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:rate",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "and integrating from the initial population ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N_0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives the exponential law",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "N(t) = N_0\\, e^{-\\lambda t}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:decay",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The constant ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the decay constant, measured in ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\mathrm{s^{-1}}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": "; the mean lifetime is its inverse, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\tau = 1/\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Half-life and activity",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "title": "Half-life",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The half-life ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "t_{1/2}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the time after which half of an initial population has decayed.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "start": true,
      "type": "Theorem"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Setting ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N = N_0/2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:decay",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "t_{1/2} = \\frac{\\ln 2}{\\lambda} \\approx 0.693\\,\\tau.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:halflife",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "What a detector counts is not ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " but the activity ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "A = \\lambda N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the number of decays per second. Its SI unit is the becquerel (1 Bq = 1 decay per second)",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The older unit, the curie, equals ",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            },
            {
              "latex": "3.7\\times10^{10}\\ \\mathrm{Bq}",
              "type": "MathInline"
            },
            {
              "text": " and is still found in clinical literature.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "Footnote"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Because ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "A \\propto N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the activity obeys the same exponential law as the population, with the same half-life.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Table ",
