    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sparse regression",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Given a design matrix ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "X \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n\\times d}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and a response ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "y \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the lasso solves",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\beta^{*} = \\arg\\min_{\\beta}\\ \\tfrac{1}{2}\\|X\\beta - y\\|_2^2 + \\lambda\\|\\beta\\|_1 ,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:lasso",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "with ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda > 0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " controlling sparsity. Least-angle regression ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "efron2004"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " traces the whole solution path but needs cubic time in the number of active features.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "First-order methods",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Coordinate descent ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "friedman2010"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " and proximal gradient methods ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "beck2009"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " avoid matrix factorisations. Accelerated proximal gradient attains the optimal ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "O(1/t^2)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " rate, but each iteration touches the full matrix.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Identified gap",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "No published solver combines a per-iteration cost proportional to the data sparsity with the accelerated rate and a guarantee on the selected support. Closing this gap is the aim of the thesis.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
