{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radioactive decay",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A. Author",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radioactive decay",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "ch:decay",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "An unstable nucleus transforms into another one at a moment that nothing in its past predicts. Yet a large sample of identical nuclei decays with perfect regularity. This chapter derives that regularity, defines the quantities used to measure it, and applies them to a medical radioisotope generator. The treatment follows the standard approach of introductory nuclear physics texts ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "example2019",
            "sample2021"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The decay law",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Suppose a sample contains ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N(t)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " nuclei at time ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "t",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Each nucleus has the same probability per unit time ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " of decaying, independent of its age and of its surroundings. In a short interval ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\mathrm{d}t",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " the number of decays is therefore proportional to the number of nuclei present,",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\frac{\\mathrm{d}N}{\\mathrm{d}t} = -\\lambda N,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:rate",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "and integrating from the initial population ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N_0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives the exponential law",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "N(t) = N_0\\, e^{-\\lambda t}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:decay",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The constant ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the decay constant, measured in ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\mathrm{s^{-1}}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": "; the mean lifetime is its inverse, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\tau = 1/\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Half-life and activity",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "title": "Half-life",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The half-life ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "t_{1/2}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the time after which half of an initial population has decayed.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "start": true,
      "type": "Theorem"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Setting ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N = N_0/2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:decay",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "t_{1/2} = \\frac{\\ln 2}{\\lambda} \\approx 0.693\\,\\tau.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:halflife",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "What a detector counts is not ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " but the activity ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "A = \\lambda N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the number of decays per second. Its SI unit is the becquerel (1 Bq = 1 decay per second)",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The older unit, the curie, equals ",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            },
            {
              "latex": "3.7\\times10^{10}\\ \\mathrm{Bq}",
              "type": "MathInline"
            },
            {
              "text": " and is still found in clinical literature.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "Footnote"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Because ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "A \\propto N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the activity obeys the same exponential law as the population, with the same half-life.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Table ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "tab:isotopes",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " lists five isotopes whose half-lives span seven orders of magnitude.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Isotope",
          "Half-life",
          "$\\lambda$ (s$^{-1}$)",
          "Typical use"
        ],
        [
          "Tc-99m",
          "6.01 h",
          "$3.20\\times10^{-5}$",
          "medical imaging"
        ],
        [
          "Po-210",
          "138 d",
          "$5.80\\times10^{-8}$",
          "static eliminators"
        ],
        [
          "I-131",
          "8.02 d",
          "$1.00\\times10^{-6}$",
          "thyroid therapy"
        ],
        [
          "Co-60",
          "5.27 y",
          "$4.17\\times10^{-9}$",
          "radiotherapy sources"
        ],
        [
          "C-14",
          "5730 y",
          "$3.83\\times10^{-12}$",
          "radiocarbon dating"
        ]
      ],
      "caption": "Half-lives and decay constants of five isotopes.",
      "label": "tab:isotopes",
      "alignment": "llrl",
      "style": "booktabs",
      "merges": [],
      "header": true,
      "repeat_header": false,
      "shading": {},
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A worked example",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "kind": "example",
      "title": "",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A therapy dose of iodine-131 has an activity of 200 MBq. How many atoms does it contain, and what is its activity after 24 days?",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "start": true,
      "type": "Theorem"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "From Table ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "tab:isotopes",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda = 1.00\\times10^{-6}\\ \\mathrm{s^{-1}}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". The number of atoms follows from the definition of activity:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "N = \\frac{A}{\\lambda} = \\frac{2.00\\times10^{8}\\ \\mathrm{s^{-1}}}{1.00\\times10^{-6}\\ \\mathrm{s^{-1}}} = 2.0\\times10^{14}.",
      "numbered": false,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "With a molar mass of 131 g/mol this is about 44 ng of iodine, an invisible quantity. After 24 days, nearly three half-lives, Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:decay",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "A(24\\ \\mathrm{d}) = 200\\ \\mathrm{MBq}\\times 2^{-24/8.02} \\approx 25\\ \\mathrm{MBq}.",
      "numbered": false,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Decay chains",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Often the product of a decay is itself radioactive. For a parent ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "1",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " that feeds a daughter ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the daughter population obeys ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\dot N_2 = \\lambda_1 N_1 - \\lambda_2 N_2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", whose solution with ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N_2(0)=0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "N_2(t) = N_1(0)\\,\\frac{\\lambda_1}{\\lambda_2-\\lambda_1}\\left(e^{-\\lambda_1 t} - e^{-\\lambda_2 t}\\right).",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:bateman",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "When the parent lives much longer than the daughter, the ratio of activities settles to a constant, a state called transient equilibrium:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\frac{A_2}{A_1} \\to \\frac{\\lambda_2}{\\lambda_2-\\lambda_1}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:equilibrium",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The technetium generator used in hospitals works this way. Molybdenum-99 (65.9 h) decays to technetium-99m (6.01 h). Inserting the two decay constants, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "0.0105\\ \\mathrm{h^{-1}}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "0.115\\ \\mathrm{h^{-1}}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " respectively, into Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:equilibrium",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives an activity ratio of about 1.1: the daughter is always slightly more active than its parent, and can be “milked” from the generator every day.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Summary",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Decay is random for one nucleus and exponential for many.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The half-life is ln 2 divided by the decay constant.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Activity decays with the population, with the same half-life.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "In a chain, the daughter reaches transient equilibrium when the parent is the longer-lived.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\begin{thebibliography}{99}\n\\bibitem{example2019} N. Example, \\emph{Introduction to Nuclear Physics}, 3rd ed. (Fictional Press, 2019).\n\\bibitem{sample2021} M. Sample and P. Placeholder, \\emph{Radioisotopes in Medicine} (Imaginary University Press, 2021).\n\\end{thebibliography}",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    }
  ],
